==Trivia==
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Baby Cat the ability to target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Baby Cat was a part of three other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Dynamites (Removed Combo)|Dynamites]], [[Baby on Board (Removed Combo)|Baby on Board]] and [[Childs Play (Removed Combo)|Childs Play]].
*Baby Cat gained [[Immune to Freeze]] in [[Version 5.3 Update|Version 5.3]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Baby Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Baby Cat
A baby Cat that still can't do anything
by itself. Luckily, daddy is there to help.
Might knockback Floating & Aliens (Area Atk)</pre>
<pre>Baby Cats
Brought along it's baby sister.
Dad has his work cut out for him.
Might knockback Floating & Aliens (Area Atk)</pre>
<pre>Cats in the Cradle
Even 7 kittens together can't do much…
Luckily Dad's still keeping an eye out for bullies.
Area wave attacks knockback Floating/Alien.</pre>
**Cats in the Stroller's description was left unchanged.
**There was a typo in its Evolved Form description, with it saying "''it's'' baby sister" instead of "'''its''' baby sister".
*The True Form name could be a reference to the Harry Chapin song "[[wikipedia:Cat's in the Cradle|Cat's in the Cradle]]".
*Interestingly enough, despite the change from 'Cradle' to 'Stroller' that Baby Cat's ultra form undergoes, they are both technically strollers. Even with that, both forms resemble cradles far more than they do strollers.
*There was a typo in Cat Babies' 3DS description, misspelling "him" as "hiim".
*According to the [[Nyanko Daisensou 4Koma & Strategy App|Nyanko Daisensou 4koma]], Baby Cat's mother is [[Kerihime (Special Cat)|Princess Punt]], while their father is very clearly [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]].
**Additionally, [[Kung Fu Cat X (Rare Cat)|Kung Fu Cat X]] is alluded to be Baby Cat's grandfather, due to the Cat Combo [[Treasured Grandchild (Combo)|Treasured Grandchild]].

